A) SMTP with OAuth2 (XOAUTH2)

What IT must do

Create an Azure AD app registration.

Grant API permissions to Exchange (“SMTP.Send” if available) or enable SMTP OAuth for your mailbox.

Share : Tenant ID, Client ID, Secret/Certificate; optionally a specific mailbox (can be your service account).

Your app must

Obtain an OAuth2 access token (client credentials or user-delegated flow).

Configure JavaMail to use XOAUTH2 (no password), e.g. set the token as the “password”.

(Implementation is fiddly; many teams skip this and use Graph instead.)

B) Microsoft Graph sendMail (recommended for OAuth2)

What IT must do

Azure AD app registration with Application permission: Mail.Send.

Admin consent granted.

(If sending as a shared mailbox) grant that app Send As or Send On Behalf right